// The last two of insn/row_fields.id's readers: the auxiliary value list
// and the home block.

chk_l() {
  int[] ret_li = ir_l((import chk_id)[0]);
} return int[] ret_li;
given ir_rows ():([])
given ir_rows_chk1 ():([])

// ihome is written both ways -- pushed as -1 when an instruction is made
// (../insn/cols.id) and lset to a real block by ir_add (../../edit/place.id)
// and m2r_front_fin (opt/mem/phi/more.id) -- but it wants no summing reader
// of the kind outv and phiof have. This one already pins which cell holds
// what, which is the stronger statement; a sum could not tell a pushed -1
// from an lset of -1 somewhere else. There is no gap here, unlike the tables
// recorded elsewhere as deliberately uncovered.
chk_home() {
  int ret_i = ir_home((import chk_id)[0]);
} return int ret_i;
given ir_rows ():(0)
given ir_rows_chk1 ():(-1)

// The most recently pushed entry of irprog (../func/more.id), for a case on
// ir_func4: its own index arithmetic is otherwise unobserved once fnname
// already has the row it counts.
chk_irprog_last() {
  int n = len((import irprog));
  int ret_i = (import irprog)[n - 1];
} return int ret_i;
given ir_rows ():(1)
given ir_rows_chk1 ():(1)
